{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Two hands for the one board.</b> Each hand is cut out on four sides, so that the edges of the board will be flush with the edges of the socket, on the inside and on the outside. And what Rashi explained — cut out on three of their sides — that is from the outer side and from the inner side and from the side facing the other board, for the groove in the middle of the board is not called the groove of the hand but rather the groove of the board." "<b>One toward its fellow.</b> What Rashi explained — that the thickness of the board is one cubit — we derive this from the two boards at the corners."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Rashi cited by the reverent abbreviation פרש״י; resolved as standard.", 1 "Rashi cited by the reverent abbreviation פרש״י; resolved as standard."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:36.685347342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}